  "summary": "Messages queue cleared under RBC-RX-05 (7 items, including one that arrived while I worked). Three new results also arrived mid-work and changed three decisions; each was corrected and recorded.\n\n**Frank Odum (pt-0027), lisinopril 10 mg:** First renewed for 90 days + 1 refill (Jan 2026 BMP, K 4.5; the Aug 2026 outside K 5.9 was hemolyzed, so a repeat BMP sr-t0002 was ordered). Then a new valid St. Brigid BMP (collected 10/20) showed K 5.8. I cancelled the renewal mr-t0001 before dispensing and sent you an urgent review task (task-t0020). The patient got a corrected message. No lisinopril order is active.\n\n**Samuel Price (pt-0030):**\n- Metformin 1000 mg BID: renewed for 90 days + 1 refill (mr-t0006). eGFR is 58 (corrected from 65), and the outside HbA1c of 7.1% from 8/19 counts. This one order answers the patient's message and both pharmacy requests.\n- Lisinopril 20 mg: first renewed. Then the 10/6 creatinine was corrected to 1.49, a 35.5% rise within 4 weeks of the dose increase, so the policy treats it like a potassium of 5.5 or higher. I cancelled the renewal mr-t0005 and sent you an urgent review task (task-t0021). The patient got a corrected message. His 30-day supply has run out and no lisinopril order is active.\n\n**Marcus Webb (pt-0031):**\n- Metformin 500 mg BID: renewed for 90 days + 1 refill (mr-t0013). The eGFR 39 from 10/14 was marked entered in error, so the most recent valid eGFR is 90 and HbA1c is 6.9%.\n- Lisinopril 10 mg: at first his last BMP was more than 12 months old, so he got 30 days + a BMP order. Then a 10/22 BMP arrived (K 4.6), and I replaced that order with 90 days + 1 refill (mr-t0019). The patient was updated.\n- The BMP order sr-t0012 is now redundant. I couldn't cancel it with my tools, so please cancel it.\n\nEach patient got a reply, and each patient has a chart note. I closed the three new results items for these patients. I did not touch the other 8 open results items, which are for other patients and outside 